    "rationale": "Pure sizing calculation for a PLINK binary genotype dataset. The .bed format packs 2 bits per sample per variant, so total size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB, and per-chromosome size uses the same rule on the largest chromosome's variant count. The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the reference build (22 autosomes + X + Y + MT = 25 for standard human builds).",
